            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carmela McCleary"
            },
            "reviewBody": "to make ur own fluff: 1 (6- or 7-ounce) jar Marshmallow Creme or Fluff = Gently heat 1 (16-ounce) package marshmallows plus 3 1/2 tablespoons light corn syrup. Gently melt in a double boiler, stirring constantly.\n\nGreat if you don't refrigerate - turns gelatinous",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-31T05:43:06.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SueandBob Butler"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i have been making a version of this for years and it is always a hit! i make it with 1 jar of marshmallow, 2 sticks of cream cheese and 1 container strawberry yogurt (regular not fruit on the bottom and not custard etc.) in addition i add 2 fresh strawberries then blend till mixed, fantastic with any fruit",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-28T14:09:02.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "missyp13"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Its a great recipe, but the 2 jars of marshmellow creme is too much for me. I always have used 1 package of cream cheese, and1 jar of marshmellow creme. Also, by putting the cream cheese in the microwave for about 20 seconds, the texture comes out much smoother. I've also always added a bit of orage zest. Once the dip has set for about an hour, the zest really brings out the flavor and adds a little something extra to the mix. I've been making it since I was about 12, and its always been a favorite.",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-24T17:58:37.517Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
